  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A youth-led ecosystem for the water sector ahead of the 10th World Water Forum, Bali 2024</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AmbitionThe ambition is to strengthen the collaboration between local knowledge and educational institutes and youth organisations. It is aimed to collaboratively initiate an &quot;Indonesia Wave&quot; and build support beyond the Netherlands for the post-World Water Forum, Bali 2024 (WWF Bali 2024) phase.The purpose of this assignment is to create and execute the &quot;Indonesia Wave&quot;, and explore its potential and possibilities for adoption by Indonesian counterparts.The &quot;Indonesia Wave&quot; aims to empower youth to work on concrete solutions for global water challenges.Scope and activitiesThe scope and activities are to effectively prepare, initiate, establish and anchor the &quot;Indonesia Wave&quot;. The assignment aims to contribute to:&#x2022;	Bringing together and building upon various existing youth and young professional networks in Indonesia into a local &apos;wave&apos;, as a concrete follow-up to the United Nations (UN) 2023 Water Conference, and linked to existing youth initiatives such as the General Assembly of the Youth Parliament for Water.&#x2022;	Identifying local champions who act as ambassador of the &quot;Indonesia Wave&quot;.&#x2022;	Exploring interest among Government of Indonesia for hosting the secretariat of the &quot;Indonesia Wave&quot; for at least one year.&#x2022;	Organizing a youth event during the WWF Bali 2024 and preparatory/runner-up activities towards WWF Bali.&#x2022;	Building support beyond the Netherlands for the post-WWF Bali 2024.More concretely, the following activities are anticipated:1.	Guest lecture and mini challenges on &quot;Design for Good&quot;.2.	Development of the &quot;Indonesian Wave&quot;, including outreach, identification of local champions and governance aspects (e.g. hosting secretariat, identification for broad support base beyond the Netherlands).3.	The &quot;Future is Now&quot; event in Bali, including the Bali &quot;Raincraft Interactive&quot; design workshop, inspirations speakers and the launch of the &quot;Indonesia Wave&quot;.NB The Dutch pavilion can be used for this event.4.	Outline for a post-WWF Bali 2024 process, including financial aspect.5.	Active communication on the various (runner-up) events and produced outcomes (e.g. workshop outcomes).</narrative>
  </description>
